#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119477 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "b25256b2-09fe-5faa-b27a-bfea7654e8ef" :question/math-academy-id "e-3019" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} [  3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) ] \\,\\textrm{d}t$ given that $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 16, \\: 2,\\: -2\\right\\rangle$ and $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2}\\mathbf g(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 2,-4,2\\right\\rangle .$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t =  \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3f(t)+g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨16,\\,2,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨48,\\,6,\\,-6⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨50,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119478 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "5c4164d7-605a-597c-9bab-f6599becc527" :question/math-academy-id "e-3020" :question/problem "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\: 1, \\: 3 \\right\\rangle$\nand\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 0, \\: 2, \\: 6 \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t+\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t = \n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t - \\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6⟩-⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119479 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "1d356bbb-b4ad-5730-9bd1-7f3cd151f96f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3021" :question/problem "Find $\\displaystyle {\\int_0^1 }  \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t)  \\, \\textrm d t$ \ngiven that \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm d t = \\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k$ \nand \n$\\mathbf c=\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k .$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t =  \\mathbf c \\times {\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t  .\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(j-k)\\times (i-3\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-4-3)i-(0+1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =-7\\,i-\\,j-\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119622 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/id #uuid "40927582-03c4-5dcb-b2cc-7c68c73388b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8688" :question/problem "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2\\mathbf f(t) + \\langle 1,\\:-1,\\:1\\rangle\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_2^0\\mathbf f(t) \\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle -3, \\: 2, \\: 1 \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨t,\\,-t,\\,t⟩{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨2,\\,-2,\\,2⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,-4,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ef1d1af-4db6-5b3b-9d5d-960b80e29691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-6,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334657} {:answer/id #uuid "02cb6977-2183-5d99-814e-766532f7f9b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-5,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334658} {:answer/id #uuid "292a30c6-436e-53cc-9ed1-7a4048ffddd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1,\\,2,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334659} {:answer/id #uuid "e17ab530-7d88-5758-91ca-92f87f20e818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-10,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334660} {:answer/id #uuid "f1572085-6e0c-5089-a44e-c5c198215dfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-8,\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e17ab530-7d88-5758-91ca-92f87f20e818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-10,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334660} :answer-field/id #uuid "800c3d62-349a-536b-adb9-bebc3271fe2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334656}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3649b2fe-dd3f-5319-9372-b19d8b8dbcb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-129140" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩$\nand \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=3{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩-⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,-6,\\,3⟩-⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-10,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334662 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5c612b5-2a78-5b30-9676-d8f252c8d7f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,3,\\,9⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334664} {:answer/id #uuid "40c6b1fc-043a-51f3-8948-15a1c325c021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,-4,\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334665} {:answer/id #uuid "b37c21ba-1e55-5c32-b4ae-4090a8e95b64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,5,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334666} {:answer/id #uuid "3628450d-8524-560c-bcc3-69f560cd2bb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,9,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334667} {:answer/id #uuid "375eae04-6f3c-590b-8049-91536355e4a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,3,\\,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3628450d-8524-560c-bcc3-69f560cd2bb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,9,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334667} :answer-field/id #uuid "edbee573-214e-55a2-acd7-b88d1dd8cc43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "884c105d-2d38-575b-867c-4a537e66762f" :question/math-academy-id "q-129143" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}[f(t)-\\frac{3}{2}g(t)]\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,6,\\,-1⟩$ and ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨1,\\,-2,\\,-6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[f(t)-\\frac{3}{2}g(t)]\\text{d}t={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[f(t)-\\frac{3}{2}g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,6,\\,-1⟩-\\frac{3}{2}⟨1,\\,-2,\\,-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,6,\\,-1⟩-⟨\\frac{3}{2}\\,-3,\\,-9⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,9,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334690 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a30f880-6499-5a68-8e7b-8ef9cc3127c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,4,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334692} {:answer/id #uuid "21944836-be42-59ed-88da-16d9ff9a49f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,-8,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334693} {:answer/id #uuid "12d81ca4-1646-5cce-881a-2a24374550eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,0,\\,12⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334694} {:answer/id #uuid "75a83e4c-a709-5311-afb0-e83cb7b58d4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,-4,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334695} {:answer/id #uuid "ec7f0748-e92b-51bb-b8b0-425a4689ecaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,-3,\\,15⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12d81ca4-1646-5cce-881a-2a24374550eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,0,\\,12⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334694} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d6f4e36-aa33-5002-82a0-e94d687d63b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "80a7d3f6-d772-5f34-8863-1998d980862c" :question/math-academy-id "q-129270" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{0}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨5,\\,1,\\,20⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨1,\\,1,\\,8⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,1,\\,20⟩-⟨1,\\,1,\\,8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,0,\\,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98f31c75-cfb3-5078-8017-f781be5519fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334706} {:answer/id #uuid "f6ba3181-f272-5b10-a279-b05934db8da6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334707} {:answer/id #uuid "bea486b9-ce9d-53ff-bcad-d7b8795a8a43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334708} {:answer/id #uuid "18056e48-a148-5750-a397-9f71b2e634b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334709} {:answer/id #uuid "3ce26c67-cfda-52e4-9f57-c8ed7a3267e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18056e48-a148-5750-a397-9f71b2e634b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334709} :answer-field/id #uuid "f96b68bd-58a7-540b-8429-0e37f49d2bcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "418288b0-73e1-53ba-989d-6a1076766b84" :question/math-academy-id "q-32300" :question/problem "Given that \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,k,$ \n$c=i+u\\,j-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,k,$\nand \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ what is the value of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i+u\\,j-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,k)\\cdot (\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}+u-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8} \\\\  & =u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ we must have $u=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334718 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06e1a8bd-192a-5d8c-911a-e177dfb7ce9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i-2j+4k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334720} {:answer/id #uuid "8574fde5-fb29-5ac6-8416-2de97bb2fc76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4i-6j+2k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334721} {:answer/id #uuid "b11c2512-97aa-5321-8629-5246aea9bddd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+2j-4k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334722} {:answer/id #uuid "a7df66a0-c3b2-540a-abf1-e56481e17e6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+6j+2k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334723} {:answer/id #uuid "ccaa5a2b-a015-56c6-ac37-5031c36333b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i-6j-4k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccaa5a2b-a015-56c6-ac37-5031c36333b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i-6j-4k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334724} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc6eede9-d55d-59ed-8257-0f817d1476ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334719}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b190b78e-5c96-53ca-a8be-8f4dce1bb987" :question/math-academy-id "q-32522" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=4\\,i+2\\,k$ \nand \n$c=i+j-k.$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i+j-k)\\times (4\\,i+2\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(2+4)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =2i-6j-4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86734ecb-63a6-548e-a852-42993ab3d2ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},\\,6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2,\\,21⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334727} {:answer/id #uuid "5b26e7a4-2aaf-5884-9a12-bffbf3a52418" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2}-7,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2+3,\\,9⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334728} {:answer/id #uuid "2b88247b-efa8-5707-8141-0471f67b3b57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{e}^{2}+3,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2+9,\\,12⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334729} {:answer/id #uuid "efcf0520-67f5-5e70-ba51-5ed3a160cb91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7{e}^{2},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2-3,\\,21⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334730} {:answer/id #uuid "597c5a08-6352-59ba-9235-d2a6dd454e89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2}+7,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2-3,\\,21⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "597c5a08-6352-59ba-9235-d2a6dd454e89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2}+7,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2-3,\\,21⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334731} :answer-field/id #uuid "59a96ac9-5380-5377-93d8-20719ba9aacf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8b8f7a3-b02e-51d2-ba01-d642e151c57b" :question/math-academy-id "q-98157" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{2}[2f(t)+3g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨{e}^{2}-1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2,\\,3⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨3,\\,-1,\\,5⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}[2f(t)+3g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=2{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+3{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[2f(t)+3g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+3{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2⟨{e}^{2}-1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2,\\,3⟩+3⟨3,\\,-1,\\,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2}-2,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2,\\,6⟩+⟨9,\\,-3,\\,15⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2}+7,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2-3,\\,21⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334767 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddd76e10-a0bf-5f83-907d-a4a7c5fb5498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,\\,14,\\,-7⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334769} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a84646-5287-5ed7-ab41-5461c13eb082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,-12,\\,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334770} {:answer/id #uuid "36adf932-fc5c-5141-ad73-55fa5c954a3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,-9,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334771} {:answer/id #uuid "bc9aaeba-ae4b-540a-bc98-c1f311496d62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,\\,-4,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334772} {:answer/id #uuid "c660023e-80e1-5ae5-9285-67938de68941" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,\\,-9,\\,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c660023e-80e1-5ae5-9285-67938de68941" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,\\,-9,\\,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334773} :answer-field/id #uuid "5613a850-8139-516d-b031-c2c2e443542e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4736ed45-f533-5962-90e0-0808ce85c132" :question/math-academy-id "q-98216" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{3}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{4}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩-⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨10,\\,-9,\\,11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334781 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a52d6fe4-983d-5fc5-abfa-852967224537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i-9\\,j-8\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334783} {:answer/id #uuid "aa14e4e8-7f9c-5bfd-a580-3d78072fb500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i+9\\,j+8\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334784} {:answer/id #uuid "3067398b-d785-5d98-80cd-aa63c7609821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-6\\,j-9\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334785} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e4e500-a6d6-5e1c-b1ba-2d1d5c878b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i-6\\,j+8\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334786} {:answer/id #uuid "705cd188-90a0-5b87-918e-7db50dcaa4a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+6\\,j+9\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa14e4e8-7f9c-5bfd-a580-3d78072fb500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i+9\\,j+8\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334784} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fa14558-5238-5a43-90a3-55a974287e74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6eb25e4-3fa7-5a49-963f-966694cb971b" :question/math-academy-id "q-98279" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{2}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=6\\,i-4\\,j+3\\,k$ \nand \n$c=i-2\\,j+2\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i-2\\,j+2\\,k)\\times (6\\,i-4\\,j+3\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-6+8)i-(3-12)j+(-4+12)k \\\\  & =2\\,i+9\\,j+8\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
